From 06383e6b2ca06d55ea6ea6380546b6a50b6390e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:12:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Release v0.5.2: tokio 1.54.1, and the notice names 0.5.2 only
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

tokio 1.54.0 is yanked: its Interval can drop a timer entry the time
driver still writes to (tokio-rs/tokio#8695, fixed in 1.54.1 by #8692),
which aborted a DHT test on main (#731). The owner chose to carry the
fix in v0.5.2 rather than cut a v0.5.1.x now (main §2.58), so this
backports #731's bump: tokio's lock entry, every requirement on 1.54.0,
the companions exact pin and the shipped licence list. cargo also
refreshes fuzz/Cargo.lock's stale 0.5.0 workspace versions to 0.5.2.

The Legal Notice's "Applies to" line on this branch said version 4
applies to main's development builds, which now carry version 5. It
now names 0.5.2 and its release candidates only (owner delegation
§2.57; the mirror image of #725). NOTICE_VERSION stays 4: the edit says
which software the notice describes, not what it does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EYhgh4JX3AmHzKXPjYCoUg
